                <pb facs="0161" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4131/10–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-11T18:00:00-05:00">October 11, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9039. On October 11 US–UK Commercial Policy Committee ratified agreed positions,
                    which had been worked out earlier in combined subcommittees, regarding <hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) procedure for holding proposed conference on
                    trade and employment in a manner designed to avoid unilateral decision by US as
                    to whether non-United Nations should be invited to conference; <hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) export taxes; <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)
                    state trading; and <hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>) subsidies. There remain for
                    consideration subjects of cartels, exchange controls, and preferences. It is
                    hoped that an agreement in subcommittee regarding first two of these will be
                    reached shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
